titre$Inocybes Gr. Paheodisca ALESSIO Generalia et Descriptiones
com$Iconographia Mycologica VoI. XXIX Supplementum III / adapt GF nov 2012

1,0$a) Cap cuticle broken up into prominent squames; cap brownish-ochraceous-rusty:$I. olivaceo-brunnea Favre *
1,2$b) Cap cuticle only with radially disconnected fibres, exceptionally with tiny squamules, in this case cap whitish-isabel-ivory
2,3$a) Cap bicoloured, i.e. differing in tinges between dise and margin
2,4$b) Cap colouration uniform, not difïerentiated zone-wise
3,0$a) Cap ochraceous at dise, greyish at margin$I. treneri Bres. (LXXIII, 2)
3,0$b) Cap brown-chestnut-tawny at dise, ochraceous at margin$I. phaeodisca Kûhn. (LXXII, 1)
4,5$a) Spore, or spores and cystidia very minute (microscopical analysis)
4,6$b) Microscopical elements of usual size ..
5,0$a) Spores and cystidia short, below typical ones in Inocybe; cap almost always with central umbo; stem slender, slim$I. microspora Lange (LXXIV, 1)
5,0$b) Spores short, but cystidia of normal size. Cap more obtuse at centre as a rule; stem almost always shorter and stouter$I. parvispora n. sp. (LXXIV, 2)
6,0$a) Cystidia shape nearly always spécial (cylindrical, with constrictions and very thin-walled)$I. leptocystîs Atk. (LXXI, 2)
6,7$b) Cystidia normally shaped
7,8$a) Cap light, traces of the early veil not permanent .
7,9$b) Cap more or less brownish, with evident remnants of the early veil persisting for différent lapses of time
8,0$a) Cap buff-ochre or brown-yellow; stem lacking pinkish tints both inside and outside .$I. subnudipes Kùhn. *
8,0$b) Cap lighter, ivory-white; stem showing an evident inner pinkish tinge in its upper portion$I. phaeodisca Kuhn. v. geophylloides Kiïhn. (LXXII, 2)
9,0$a) Small size. Stem lacking pinkish tones in any life stage$I. abjecta Karst. (LXXIII, 1)
9,0$b) Larger size. Stem upper région fleshy-pink, at least in the juvenile stage ....$I. griseovelata Kùhn. *
